<!-- ============ PAST EVENTS ============ -->
<section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Past Events</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Where TeamworkCares started.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="past-grid">
      <div class="past-card">
        <img src="/assets/images/company/cares/shoes-that-fit.webp" alt="Shoes donated through the Shoes that Fit program" loading="lazy">
        <div class="past-body">
          <h3>Shoes that Fit</h3>
          <p>We collaborated with Shoes that Fit to provide over 75 pairs of shoes to a local elementary school so students can attend school in comfort.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="past-card">
        <img src="/assets/images/company/cares/blm-5k.webp" alt="Participants in the BLM Virtual Strides 5K" loading="lazy">
        <div class="past-body">
          <h3>BLM Virtual Strides 5K</h3>
          <p>We kicked off the launch of TeamworkCares with the BLM Virtual Strides 5K. We had over 40 participants from around the world participate in a Black Lives Matter virtual 5K that helped to raise money for the United Negro College Foundation, dedicated to helping more African American students attend and graduate from college.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="past-card">
        <img src="/assets/images/company/cares/kharkiv.webp" alt="Medical supplies purchased for hospitals in Kharkiv" loading="lazy">
        <div class="past-body">
          <h3>Kharkiv medical sphere</h3>
          <p>We supported the Kharkiv medical sphere over several months. The company purchased two Microlife BP AG1-30 arterial pressure meters and a microwave oven for Children's Regional Clinical Hospital, and equipment for the 40-seat oxygen route and 14 beds in intensive care for the Regional Clinical Infectious Disease Hospital. The company also participated in the acquisition of a biochemical analyzer for the same hospital, and in December bought New Year gifts for the children of deceased soldiers.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="past-card">
        <img src="/assets/images/company/cares/lunchpals.webp" alt="Students in a LunchPals mentoring session" loading="lazy">
        <div class="past-body">
          <h3>LunchPals</h3>
          <p>The TeamworkCares Mentorship Committee recruited student mentor volunteers and helped match them to mentor kids from schools in underserved communities in Pinellas County. We worked with LunchPals and matched up 15 volunteer mentors that met weekly with kids, providing emotional support, lending a listening ear, and running fun learning activities. LunchPals aims to build emotional resilience and confidence in kids to perform better in school.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="past-card" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;">
        <img src="/assets/images/company/cares/mystuffbags.webp" alt="Duffel bags filled with belongings for the MyStuffBags charity drive" loading="lazy" style="aspect-ratio: 32/9;">
        <div class="past-body">
          <h3>MyStuffBags</h3>
          <p>As part of back to school, TeamworkCares participated in the MyStuffBags charity drive to provide new belongings to children living in shelters, rescued from abuse, neglect, abandonment, and homelessness. MyStuffBags provides children across the United States with duffel bags and backpacks filled with items such as toys, blankets, clothing, coloring books, school supplies and toiletries, with the goal of providing new belongings to each of the nearly 300,000 children each year who must enter crisis shelters and foster care with nothing of their own.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

